<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Liénard de l'Olive</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Liénard de l'Olive was a French colonist who, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-du-plessis-dossonville">Jean du Plessis d'Ossonville</a>, led the first French settlement of Guadeloupe in June 1635 for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/compagnie-des-iles-de-lamerique">Compagnie des Îles de l'Amérique</a>. The settlers suffered famine and disease, and after du Plessis died he governed the colony alone and waged a harsh war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinago">Kalinago</a> inhabitants. He was later replaced as governor by Jean Aubert.</p></div>
